#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:5
#: 99fe127a7a764ac1929524261bae565d
msgid "Simple and Super Simple Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:7
#: d2ad0704def6457bb6e583b90b68de1f
msgid ""
"This article describes the behaviour of the *Simple* and *Super Simple* "
"modes and explains how you can set up selection of these modes from your "
"RC Transmitter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:12
#: 79732f289d0d49a5a51be0720b837699
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:14
#: b0d9ff8cae2f4835a503c6f99be7ae32
msgid ""
"\"Simple\" and \"Super Simple\" modes allow the pilot to control the "
"movement of the copter from the pilot's point of view regardless of which"
" way the copter is facing. This is useful for new pilots who have not "
"mastered adjusting their roll and pitch inputs depending upon which way "
"the vehicle is facing and for cases when the copter is far enough away "
"that it's heading is not apparent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:21
#: 148e3f8488794096a2b0adbefd0db78f
msgid ""
"\"Simple\" and \"Super Simple\" modes can be used in combination with "
"nearly all flight modes except the Acro and Drift (in these flight modes "
"the setting is ignored)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:24
#: 394741c30c5c452f9cb5f69d8ce77d03
msgid ""
"Simple Mode allows you to control the copter relative to the copters "
"heading at take off and relies only on a good compass heading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:26
#: 82d0b559786e43129ef0a1d1800d640c
msgid ""
"Super Simple Mode allows you to control the copter relative to it's "
"direction from home (i.e. where it was armed) but requires a good GPS "
"position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:29
#: e60ab1da29cd4cdc90f5a1dad2c02a23
msgid ""
"Either mode can be assigned to a particular flight mode switch position "
"or can be enabled/disabled from the :ref:`Ch7/Ch8 switches "
"<channel-7-and-8-options>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:36
#: 4f8592d980e04ace97617dfba05262a1
msgid "Normal Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:41
#: 20400730196941e1b956bada0e920ff8
msgid ""
"Without Simple or Super Simple enabled, the pilot's transmitter stick "
"inputs are applied in the orientation of the copter.  For example in the "
"diagram above when the pilot applies roll input right (red) the vehicle "
"rolls to it's right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:46
#: 0b8d238e68034a3098b258acdbacc853
msgid ""
"With the copter is facing in the same direction as the pilot, it is "
"relatively easy to control the vehicle but when the vehicle is facing "
"towards the pilot an inexperienced pilot will feel that the controls are "
"all reversed.  I.e. if the pilot inputs right roll, the vehicle will move"
" to the left from the pilot's point of view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:55
#: 6c89f831893045aba11d60c613e12281
msgid "Simple Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:60
#: 7d6dcf3f30254171b49a3c4e607bfad3
msgid ""
"Similar to the \"care free\" mode on other systems, this mode allows you "
"to fly your copter as though it were pointed in the direction it was "
"pointed when it was armed regardless of its current heading orientation."
"  So if you hold the pitch stick forward the copter will fly away from "
"you, pull the pitch stick back and it will come back towards home.  You "
"can even apply yaw to spin the copter in any direction but the movement "
"of the copter's position relative to the stick inputs will behave exactly"
" as it did at take off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:69
#: 36f383b431134fe8a46cabdb89c3b429
msgid ""
"Generally when arming you should stand behind the vehicle with it's nose "
"pointing directly away from you.  While flying you should try to keep the"
" vehicle flying in front of it's starting position because if it flies "
"behind you all the controls will feel reversed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:74
#: da154de2a1c24fb08937b87373a40626
msgid ""
"As mentioned above simple mode is also very useful in emergency "
"situations where the copter is far enough away that it is very difficult "
"to determine it's heading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:81
#: 3ffac00a4ce4481fb75fa34d4dfc5ad6
msgid "Super Simple Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:86
#: ab7be27fc5a54e77a271e7c75a0a89ee
msgid ""
"Super Simple mode is the same as simple mode except that it uses the "
"vehicle's position relative to home instead of the vehicle's initial "
"heading when it was armed. This means that no matter where the vehicle "
"is, pulling the pitch back will cause it to return towards home "
"regardless of the vehicle's actual heading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:92
#: 63a203117de74048a3e9b490110b73dd
msgid ""
"The advantage over simple mode is that the controls are applied from the "
"pilot's point of view even when the copter flies behind the pilot/home "
"location."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:96
#: 9380036c8a8b486ba0ffd4592dcd7d64
msgid ""
"If the pilot holds full right roll the vehicle will fly a circle "
"clockwise around the pilot (although the circle's radius may tend to grow"
" slightly with each orbit due to \"lag\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:100
#: 5d60137508e64943b1b61abe8b831bd8
msgid ""
"The disadvantage is that mode require a GPS lock because so you should "
"ensure you have GPS lock before take-off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:103
#: fb9f58c5d6774e4d93e673e5e8422c64
msgid ""
"The orientation is not updated when the vehicle is within 10m of home "
"meaning close fly-bys of the home location should be avoided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:106
#: f0b0764f6685498f8b4ebd1a1f6de214
msgid ""
"To ensure the controls are correct right at take-off, as with simple "
"mode, you should arm with the pilot standing behind the vehicle and with "
"both pilot and vehicle pointing in the same direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:111
#: a0dfb0531ee34a9195f1a07bb4db18f9
msgid "Selecting the modes from a transmitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:113
#: 9b29c39f7aeb4388a2bbf2ea3d555e64
msgid ""
"The transmitter’s :ref:`auxiliary channels <channel-7-and-8-options>` can"
" be set-up to enable selection of Simple mode, Super Simple mode or both."
" Only one auxiliary channel should be set for these modes, and this "
"channel will override the simple/super-simple options selected on the "
"Flight Modes screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:122
#: 1133bd0915564bf1ab00054e42513fb2
msgid "Mission Planner: Channel 7 options for Simple andSuperSimple modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/simpleandsuper-simple-modes.rst:124
#: bf52c967d5a04b60bf0bdf5ba3a5aa10
msgid ""
"To support selection of just one of the modes from the transmitter, "
"assign the mode to a channel that is mapped to a 2-position switch (high "
"= enables the selected mode, low disables it). To enable both modes from "
"the same switch, select *Super Simple mode* for a channel that is mapped "
"to a 3-position switch (high position = Super Simple mode, middle "
"position = Simple mode, low position = disabled)."
msgstr ""

